15. From Reactive Railway Safety to Predictive Prevention
The evolution of railway safety technology can be viewed in five stages:

Stage 1 — Paper-Based Safety
Forms, registers and manual reports.

Stage 2 — Digital Safety
Electronic inspections, incidents and audits.

Stage 3 — Connected EHS
Incidents, inspections, risks, audits and corrective actions become connected.

Stage 4 — Intelligent EHS
AI identifies patterns and provides decision support.

Stage 5 — Predictive Safety Intelligence
Organizations use connected historical and operational data to identify emerging risk signals and strengthen preventive controls.

The objective is not to remove humans from safety management.

It is to help safety professionals see more, understand faster and act earlier.

